{%- comment -%}
  Wavy top edge for a section. Renders an SVG wave filled with `color`, absolutely
  positioned to sit just above the section and overlap the section before it — so
  each section paints its own wave over whatever color came before it, with no
  need to know that neighbor's color. The parent section needs position: relative
  (and no overflow: hidden clipping its top) for this to show correctly; both are
  handled by each section's own .wave-top-host rule.

  Usage: {%- render 'wave-divider', color: section.settings.background_color -%}
  as the very first thing inside the section, right after its opening tag.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="section-wave-top" aria-hidden="true">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 1200 60" preserveAspectRatio="none">
    <path d="M0,32 C120,58 220,4 360,26 C500,48 580,10 720,20 C880,32 960,54 1080,30 C1140,18 1180,14 1200,18 L1200,60 L0,60 Z" fill="{{ color }}"></path>
  </svg>
</div>

<style>
  .section-wave-top { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 34px; transform: translateY(-99%); pointer-events: none; line-height: 0; z-index: 1; }
  .section-wave-top svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }
  @media (min-width: 700px) { .section-wave-top { height: 54px; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) { .section-wave-top svg path { transition: fill .3s ease; } }
</style>
